  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jagdish Dhakad vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 11 April, 2022 Author: Rajeev Kumar Shrivastava Bench: Rajeev Kumar Shrivastava 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Mcrc No. 16806 of 2022 (Jagdish Dhakad Vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh) Dated : 11-04-2022 Shri S.S.Dhakad, counsel for the applicant. Shri Manish Naik, Panel lawyer, for the respondent/State. This is Eighth application under Section 439 of CrPC for grant of bail.",
    "facts": "This is Eighth application under Section 439 of CrPC for grant of bail. His earlier applications were dismissed on merits vide order dated 8.9.2021 and 21.2.2022 passed in M.Cr.C.No.44365 of 2021 and 1300 of 2022. The applicant has been arrested on 4.1.2021 in connection with Crime No. 3/2021 registered at Police Station Pahadgarh district Morena, for the offences punishable under Sections 420, 272, 273 of IPC and 51, 57, 59 and 62 of Food Safety Act and standard Act, 2006. It is submitted by the counsel for the applicant that the applicant has been falsely implicated.",
    "arguments": "It is further submitted that two prosecution witnesses have been examined before the trial court but they have not supported the case of prosecution. From the date of last rejection, further one and half months custody has been suffered by the applicant and now, he is in custody since 4.1.2021. There is no progress in trial. Therefore, considering the custody period which is around 16 months and the offences which are triable by JMFC, he prayed for grant of bail. Per contra, the State counsel has vehemently opposed the application stating that earlier applications of the applicant were dismissed on merits and since that dates, there is no change in circumstances. Hence, considering the nature of offence, he prays for rejection of this bail application. He further submits that as per letter of subordinate court No. 82/22, Jaura dated 10.2.2022, present case has been sent to the court of CJM, Morena and the trial is pending there.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "It is further submitted that two prosecution witnesses have been examined before the trial court but they have not supported the case of prosecution. From the date of last rejection, further one and half months custody has been suffered by the applicant and now, he is in custody since 4.1.2021. There is no progress in trial. Therefore, considering the custody period which is around 16 months and the offences which are triable by JMFC, he prayed for grant of bail. Per contra, the State counsel has vehemently opposed the application stating that earlier applications of the applicant were dismissed on merits and since that dates, there is no change in circumstances. Hence, considering the nature of offence, he prays for rejection of this bail application. He further submits that as per letter of subordinate court No. 82/22, Jaura dated 10.2.2022, present case has been sent to the court of CJM, Morena and the trial is pending there.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
